4
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:24,000
Very recently this report came across my desk.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,880
It is from a bunch of very dedicated scouters studying different things about camping and

6
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:36,120
scouting at the Large Baden Collider in Zern, Switzerland,

7
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:42,680
And they have just completed a series of experiments that have determined there is

8
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:46,519
actually what is called a tootin common effect.

9
00:00:46,519 --> 00:00:49,040
That's right, a tootin common effect,

10
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:56,320
And that is that the urgency with which a person sleeping in a mummy sleeping bag

11
00:00:56,320 --> 00:01:03,440
must exit the mummy sleeping bag is in inverse proportion to the air temperature

12
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:07,680
and the degree of difficulty in operating the bag's zipper.

13
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:08,720
It's official,

14
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:09,680
It's science.

15
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,920
What can I say?

16
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:14,920
Hey, this is podcast number 310..

17
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:15,420
Hey,

18
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:43,620
Welcome back to the Scoutmaster podcast.

